{"name":"Irphong","status":"ok","title":"Irphong","pageId":107475,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Irphong</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Island</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Nelanther_Isles\" title=\"Nelanther Isles\">Nelanther Isles</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><br>\nThis lifeless island was used as a marker to show the northern end of <span class=\"new\" title=\"Asavir’s Channel (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXNhdmlyJUUyJTgwJTk5c19DaGFubmVsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Asavir’s Channel</span>. It's only notable feature is one of the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_Towers\" title=\"Sea Towers\">Sea Towers</a> was built on the cliff face of the north shore, 150 feet above the sea. Magical light emanates from the tower preventing ships from crashing into the islands or the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Dragon's Head Peninsula (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRHJhZ29uJTI3c19IZWFkX1Blbmluc3VsYT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Dragon's Head Peninsula</span>. <sup id=\"cite_ref-tethyr-p95_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tethyr-p95-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Rumors_.26_Legends\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rumors_&_Legends\">Rumors &amp; Legends</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Rumors & Legends\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Irphong?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Rumors & Legends\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>No one willingly approaches the island as it is said that the <a href=\"/wiki/Curse_of_Irphong\" title=\"Curse of Irphong\">Curse of Irphong</a> will find those that do. Whenever a pirate puts down anchor here or even approaches the shoals around it, the ship is cursed to sink within a tenday.<sup id=\"cite_ref-tethyr-p95_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tethyr-p95-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Irphong?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Irphong?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span clas